  "body": "It would be very helpful to have a way to leave maintenance notes in a static way, e.g. by placing a static json file under `/_matrix/sync` or whatever endpoint riot typically looks at.\r\n\r\nThere are two use cases for this:\r\n1) leaving a note to decommission a homeserver more gracefully than connection error / timeout\r\n2) informing users during a maintenance window where an actual synapse server isn't available\r\n\r\nMy concrete use case is that my homeserver has a downtime due to server problems, and I would be able to divert traffic to inform users of the reasons but I can't actually get synapse up. As is, people get an unhelpful \"Connection error\" on riot-web or worse, \"Riot is using battery\" on riot-android.\r\n\r\nI reckon this should be simple to spec and implement, and goes a long way towards smoothing over common error modes.",
